title: "Jekyll/Liquid variables scopes issues"
date: 2018-12-20 18:23:09 +0100
description: >
  Liquid is not a programming language!
  Take care on the use of variables...
image: https://jekyllrb.com/img/logo-2x.png
categories: [jekyll]
---

When dealing with [Jekyll][1] template and use of [Liquid][2] language one may take care when assing variables, especially with several includes.
Indeed, variables defined in a template (e.g. in `_includes`) remain defined in the parent scope.
Let consider the following basic snippet code:


```{liquid}
{% raw %}{% include templateA %}
... some stuffs...
{% include templateB %}
... other things...
use {{item}}{% endraw %}
```


 with in templateA:

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% assign item='foo'%}
{% endraw %}
```

and  templateB:

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% assign item='boo'%}
{% endraw %}
```

should output `use boo`.

This seems obvious, but in some advanced template design this [**must be**]{.text-danger} kept in mind!

Let consider a slightly better example:

```liquid
{% raw %}
{%assign collection=page.collection%}
{%assign collection_list=site.collections| where: "label", collection %}

{%for item in collection_list %}
{% assign title=item.title%}
...
{% include do-something %}
...
Use title: {{title}}
{%enfor %}
{% endraw %}
```

```liquid
{% raw %}
...
{% assign title=page.title%}
...
{%for item in others %}
...
Another use of title: {{title}}
...
{%enfor %}
{% endraw %}
```

Secondly, one should take care when using forloop variables: its seems that we should avoid reassign them...

[1]: https://jekyllrb.com "Transform your plain text into static websites and blogs"

[2]: https://shopify.github.io/liquid/ " Liquid is a templating language to process templates."
